  "answer": "The test uses `bun:test` and expects `tokens('')` → `[]` and `tokens(' a, ,b ,,c ')` → `['a','b','c']`. The current implementation just splits on commas — no trimming or empty filtering. Let me run the test first to confirm the failure:\nTest fails as expected. Now the repair — trim each token and drop empties, keeping the signature:\nRepair verified. Summary:\n\n**Before:** `bun test` failed — `tokens('')` returned `[\"\"]` instead of `[]`, and spaced/empty tokens weren't handled.\n\n**Repair in `src/tokens.ts`** (signature `tokens(value: string)` unchanged):\n```ts\nexport function tokens(value: string) { return value.split(',').map(t => t.trim()).filter(t => t.length > 0) }\n```\n\n**After:** `bun test` → **1 pass, 0 fail** (3 `expect()` calls all green), covering `tokens('')` → `[]`, `tokens(' a, ,b ,,c ')` → `['a','b','c']`, and `tokens('single')` → `['single']`.\n\n`test/oracle.test.ts`, `AGENTS.md`, and `package.json` were left untouched."
